{"schema_version":1,"search_id":"a8a3734265d54d2f9d5c1c3bdde86094","seq":21,"turn":0,"at_ms":22632.35691700538,"type":"search_finished","result":{"question":{"content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Did last month's latency spike come from the new reranker, and is it fixed?"}]},"hits":[{"hit":{"doc_id":"PR-1187","source":"pull_requests","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Roll out reranker v2 to all search traffic\n\nThis turns on reranker v2 (the cross-encoder model) for 100% of search requests, up from the 5% experiment. Offline NDCG@10 is +4.1% over v1. Batch size is set to 64 to keep GPU utilisation high. Rollout is behind the reranker_v2 flag so we can turn it off. Reviewers: @lortiz @pramam."}],"metadata":{"number":1187,"merged":"2026-09-12","service":"search-api","author":"Marcus Chen","title":"Roll out reranker v2 to all search traffic"},"raw_score":0.6295955411460765,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":7}]},"score":0.495576,"p_relevant":0.5,"rationale":"Rolls out reranker v2 to all traffic; potential cause of latency.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"PR-1165","source":"pull_requests","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"Reranker v2 experiment at 5%\n\nRaises the reranker v2 experiment from 1% to 5%. Experiment p95 latency +9 ms at 5%."}],"metadata":{"number":1165,"merged":"2026-08-31","service":"search-api","author":"Marcus Chen","title":"Reranker v2 experiment at 5%"},"raw_score":0.986053408104363,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c1","rank":3}]},"score":0.318425,"p_relevant":0.3,"rationale":"Mentions reranker v2 experiment latency impact.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4821","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"search-api p95 elevated across all regions\n\nOpened by on-call (Priya Raman) at 09:12 UTC after the SLO burn alert fired. search-api p95 latency climbed from ~180 ms to ~640 ms starting early Sept 14 and is holding there. p50 is only slightly up. Error rate is flat, so requests succeed but slowly. CPU on the search-api pods is up ~35%. Checked the CDN and the edge cache: both look normal. No config pushes in the last 12 hours. Mitigation so far: scaled search-api from 24 to 36 pods, which took p95 down to ~520 ms but did not clear it. Root cause: not yet identified. Leaving open for the search team to investigate on Monday. Customer impact: slower search results pages, some timeouts on the mobile app's type-ahead."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-09-14","service":"search-api","severity":"SEV2","status":"resolved","title":"search-api p95 elevated across all regions"},"raw_score":0.6489217206265213,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c3","rank":5},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c5","rank":1}]},"score":0.186944,"p_relevant":0.1,"rationale":"General search-api latency incident, but root cause not identified here.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4639","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"recs-api slow responses during sale\n\nrecs-api p95 latency reached 1.4 s during the flash sale start. Feature store reads were the bottleneck. Added a read replica."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-08-02","service":"recs-api","severity":"SEV3","status":"resolved","title":"recs-api slow responses during sale"},"raw_score":1.5479756184268114,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c3","rank":2},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c5","rank":0}]},"score":0.1,"p_relevant":0.0,"rationale":"Irrelevant recs incident.","judged":true},{"hit":{"doc_id":"INC-4915","source":"incidents","content":[{"kind":"text","text":"auth-gateway elevated latency\n\nauth-gateway p95 latency doubled to 220 ms for an hour because of a noisy neighbour on the shared Redis. Moved session reads to the dedicated cluster."}],"metadata":{"opened":"2026-10-09","service":"auth-gateway","severity":"SEV3","status":"resolved","title":"auth-gateway elevated latency"},"raw_score":2.091746326918598,"provenance":[{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c3","rank":1},{"turn":0,"call_id":"t0.c5","rank":2}]},"score":0.099181,"p_relevant":0.0,"rationale":"Irrelev